<!--
    Every word the app says, in one place.

    Lower case throughout, on purpose: WP8 set page titles, headers and list rows in lower case and
    that is part of the look, not a typo. A translation should keep it wherever the target language's
    orthography allows.

    Adding a language means one folder — values-ru/strings.xml and so on — and nothing else; there is
    no user-visible literal left in the Kotlin. Counts go through <plurals> rather than through
    "%d songs", because "2 песни" and "5 песен" are different forms and a format string cannot know
    that.
-->
